@@ -80,6 +80,16 @@ The options are the upstream script's (`-h`). Only `--platform ios` exists here.
 - **Xcode 27's `.xip`** is a sorted, deduplicated cpio (Metadata `xbs_sortcpio`). Only one entry of each hard-linked inode carries the bytes; the others hold a `NULLcanary` placeholder of the same size. `extract_xip.py` reads the archive twice: the first pass finds the entry that carries each inode's bytes, the second writes them to every SDK path. The extractor also resolves symlinks that point through other symlinks (`Headers → Versions/Current/Headers`).
 - **Line endings:** the checkout must keep LF (see `.gitattributes`). The shader chain hashes source bytes, so a CRLF checkout breaks `dmsh_xlate --source-sha`.
 
+### The window as an exe
+
+`Build-IPA-GUI.bat` needs Python's folder on PATH. `win/gui_launcher` builds a native `Build-IPA-GUI.exe` (Go, standard library only) that does the same job with friendlier failures: it looks pythonw.exe up in `NXW_PYTHONW`, then on PATH, then in Python's default install folders (newest version wins), then through the `py` launcher, and shows a message box instead of a console error when Python is missing or the exe was moved out of the repository root. The window it starts is still `win/gui.pyw` with the machine's Python, so the pipeline behaves exactly as when the `.bat` starts it. It cross-compiles from Linux (and builds natively on Windows with `GO111MODULE=off`):
+
+```
+CGO_ENABLED=0 GO111MODULE=off GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build -trimpath -ldflags="-s -w -H=windowsgui" -o Build-IPA-GUI.exe ./win/gui_launcher
+```
+
+`win/gui_launcher/icon.ico` (the window's black-and-pink play triangle) is embedded through `rsrc_windows_amd64.syso`; rebuild that file with `go run github.com/akavel/rsrc@latest -ico icon.ico -o rsrc_windows_amd64.syso` after changing the icon. `go test ./win/gui_launcher` (any OS, `GO111MODULE=off`) covers the Python lookup's precedence.
